,0.6156,0.0352,0.0281]},{"n":"Mona","r":[0.0815,0.6741,0.0352,0.0281]},{"n":"Columbina","r":[0.1241,0.6741,0.0352,0.0281]},{"n":"Ineffa","r":[0.1667,0.6741,0.0352,0.0281]},{"n":"Lauma","r":[0.2093,0.6741,0.0352,0.0281]}]}]}},"thumb":"content/genshin/builds/mona/261111-225142/en-1.t.webp","why":{"w":[{"name":"The Widsith","text":"CRIT DMG and huge short-window buffs suit her Burst nuke; its random buff and 30s cooldown make damage inconsistent. Burst-nuke DPS; less reliable for repeated rotations."},{"name":"Skyward Atlas","text":"High base ATK and ATK% provide consistent personal damage without depending on a random buff. Personal-damage builds."},{"name":"Lost Prayer to the Sacred Winds","text":"CRIT Rate is useful, but its stacking Elemental DMG passive needs extended field time. Primarily an on-field Mona build."},{"name":"Favonius Codex","text":"Energy Recharge and CRIT-triggered particles help fund her costly Burst and support the entire team. Land on-field CRIT hits; build adequate CRIT Rate."},{"name":"Thrilling Tales of Dragon Slayers","text":"R5 grants a major ATK buff to the character switched in next. Lacks ER, so Burst uptime can be difficult. ATK-scaling carry; 20s buff cooldown. R5 strongly preferred."},{"name":"Prototype Amber","text":"Refunds Energy after Burst and adds team healing, substantially lowering her demanding ER needs. Support or healer-lite setups. Higher refinements improve energy and healing."},{"name":"Solar Pearl","text":"CRIT Rate and a Normal Attack-activated Burst DMG buff help damage-focused builds. Use a Normal Attack before Burst to activate its passive."},{"name":"Mappa Mare","text":"Craftable EM weapon with reaction-triggered Elemental DMG stacks; useful for budget Vaporize nukes. Mona must trigger reactions; less useful for pure Omen support."}],"a":[{"names":["Emblem of Severed Fate"],"text":"Strong Burst-nuke set: converts required Energy Recharge into Burst DMG.","stats":"ATK%/ER · Hydro DMG · CRIT"},{"names":["Noblesse Oblige","Heart of Depth"],"text":"2pc Burst DMG plus 2pc Hydro DMG for a balanced nuke set; no 4pc effects are active.","stats":"ATK%/EM · Hydro DMG · CRIT"},{"names":["Noblesse Oblige"],"text":"Support option: using Burst grants the whole party 20% ATK for 12s; avoid duplicate Noblesse holders.","stats":"ER · Hydro DMG · CRIT/ATK%"}],"t":[{"name":"Frostbound Prophecy","members":["Mona","Skirk","Furina","Escoffier"],"text":"Mona's Omen amplifies Skirk's damage; Furina adds Hydro and buffs while Escoffier heals and shreds Cryo/Hydro RES. ER needs can be high.","roles":["Buffer / Hydro Enabler","On-field DPS","Off-field DPS / Buffer","Healer / Debuffer"]},{"name":"Morgana Starfall","members":["Mona","Ganyu","Venti","Diona"],"text":"Classic Freeze AoE team. Cryo and Mona's Hydro help sustain Freeze and prolong Omen; Venti groups foes and Diona sustains.","roles":["t","On-field DPS","Crowd Control / Debuffer","Shielder / Healer"]},{"name":"Hexerei Flamecraft","members":["Mona","Durin","Xingqiu","Sucrose"],"text":"Mona drives Hydro for Durin's off-field Pyro Vaporize; Xingqiu stabilizes Hydro. With Witch's Homework, Mona and Sucrose enable Hexerei synergy.","roles":["Buffer / Hydro Enabler","Off-field DPS / Buffer","Off-field DPS / Hydro Enabler","EM Buffer / Debuffer"]},{"name":"Moonlit Divination","members":["Mona","Columbina","Ineffa","Lauma"],"text":"A Lunar-reaction setup: Mona's Omen and support gear help Columbina, while Ineffa enables Lunar-Charged and Lauma adds reaction support.","roles":["Buffer / Hydro Enabler","Off-field DPS / Buffer","Off-field DPS / Shielder","Dendro Buffer / Enabler"]}],"v":"Omen Support: 4pc Noblesse, Favonius Codex or R5 TTDS; prioritize ER to Burst each rotation. Omen buffs the next damage window.\nHexerei Buffer: 4pc Celestial Gift with another Hexerei ally and Witch's Homework completed; use Normal Attacks to extend Omen.\nFreeze Support: 4pc Noblesse + Favonius/TTDS; pair with Cryo and Hydro to exploit extended Omen on frozen, unshattered enemies.\nC6 Charged DPS: 4pc A Day Carved From Rising Winds; ATK/Hydro/CRIT, strong Pyro support, and Omen-boosted Charged Attacks.\nBudget Support: Favonius or craftable Prototype Amber with 4pc Noblesse; solve Energy Recharge before chasing personal damage.","n":2},"seo":{"roles":["Burst DPS / Buffer"],"about":"Mona is a Hydro Burst nuker and Omen buffer whose Burst amplifies damage enemies take. Her Skill briefly taunts and applies Hydro, but cannot sustain most Vaporize carries alone. With another Hexerei teammate and Witch's Homework completed, her attacks can extend Omen and enhance Vaporize.","pros":["Powerful Omen damage buff","High Burst nuke potential","Hexerei synergy","Flexible support weapons"],"cons":["Very high Burst ER needs","Limited off-field Hydro","Short base Omen duration","Setup-sensitive Vaporize"],"weapons":["The Widsith","Skyward Atlas","Lost Prayer to the Sacred Winds","Favonius Codex","Thrilling Tales of Dragon Slayers","Prototype Amber","Solar Pearl","Mappa Mare"],"arts":[{"sets":["Emblem of Severed Fate"],"pcs":"4 pcs","role":"Best"},{"sets":["Noblesse Oblige","Heart of Depth"],"pcs":"2 + 2 pcs","role":""},{"sets":["Noblesse Oblige"],"pcs":"4 pcs","role":"Support"}],"main":["Energy Recharge / ATK% / Elemental Mastery","Hydro DMG","CRIT Rate / CRIT DMG"],"stats":["CRIT Rate: 60% - 75% (DPS)","CRIT DMG: 120% - 180%+ (DPS)","Energy Recharge: 180% - 300%+ (support varies)","Energy Recharge: 150% - 230% (Favonius; varies)","Energy Recharge: 120% - 180% (Amber; varies)"],"vars":[{"title":"Omen Support","role":"Support","weapons":["Favonius Codex","Thrilling Tales of Dragon Slayers","Prototype Amber"],"arts":[{"sets":["Noblesse Oblige"],"pcs":"4 pcs"},{"sets":["Tenacity of the Millelith"],"pcs":"4 pcs"}],"stats":"ER until Burst every rotation; use CRIT Rate with Favonius. Personal damage is secondary.","teams":"Bring a carry who deals damage during Omen; TTDS works best with an ATK-scaling carry.","when":"Prioritize teamwide damage rather than Mona's Bubble pop. Swap to the carry after setting up Omen.","cond":"TTDS needs sufficient ER and proper swap order; do not duplicate Noblesse.","notes":"ER can exceed 250% in solo-Hydro teams. Prototype Amber reduces requirements.","pre":false},{"title":"Hexerei Omen Buffer","role":"Support","weapons":["Favonius Codex","Thrilling Tales of Dragon Slayers","Prototype Amber"],"arts":[{"sets":["Celestial Gift"],"pcs":"4 pcs"},{"sets":["Noblesse Oblige"],"pcs":"4 pcs"}],"stats":"ER first, then Favonius CRIT Rate; Hydro DMG and CRIT are optional personal-damage stats.","teams":"Needs another Hexerei teammate and completion of Witch's Homework to activate Mona's extra passive.","when":"Use Normal/Charged hits during the setup to extend Omen and, in Vaporize teams, build Astral Glow stacks.","cond":"Requires Witch's Homework and at least one other Hexerei character.","notes":"Celestial Gift is usually her preferred Hexerei support set unless another teammate already carries it.","pre":false},{"title":"Freeze Omen Support","role":"Support","weapons":["Favonius Codex","Thrilling Tales of Dragon Slayers","Prototype Amber"],"arts":[{"sets":["Noblesse Oblige"],"pcs":"4 pcs"},{"sets":["Tenacity of the Millelith"],"pcs":"4 pcs"}],"stats":"Prioritize enough ER for every Burst; TTDS can increase ER demands.","teams":"Use strong Cryo application; pair a Freeze carry such as Ganyu or Skirk with sustain/energy support.","when":"Apply Cryo before Mona's Burst when attempting Freeze-based Bubble extension. Shatter breaks the setup.","cond":"Best against freezable enemies; bosses and Shatter limit extended Omen.","notes":"Mona's Skill alone cannot replace a sustained Hydro applicator in every team.","pre":false},{"title":"C6 Charged Attack DPS","role":"On-field DPS","weapons":["The Widsith","Skyward Atlas","Lost Prayer to the Sacred Winds","Solar Pearl"],"arts":[{"sets":["A Day Carved From Rising Winds"],"pcs":"4 pcs"},{"sets":["Heart of Depth"],"pcs":"4 pcs"}],"stats":"ATK% or EM 